    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** with 1/1 passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field so a fetched owner returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the same pattern the existing `displayName` field already uses:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it serializes into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `initials` that computes `upper(firstName[0]) + \".\" + upper(lastName[0]) + \".\"`.\n\nThe `@NotEmpty` constraint on `firstName`/`lastName` (in `Person`) plus the controller's blank-field rejection guarantee both names are non-empty before mapping, so `charAt(0)` is safe. The acceptance test (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full suite pass.",
